---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="PENGO Workbench | Pengo Systems"
  description="Important updates, recently added reference material, and useful paths into the Workbench."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/"
  active=""
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <p class="wb-type-label">Workbench home</p>
    <h1>PENGO Workbench</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Important updates, recently added reference material, and useful paths into the Workbench.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-section">
      <h2>Latest</h2>
      <div class="wb-highlight-list">
        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/start-here/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Start</p>
          <h2>Start Here</h2>
          <p>Understand why AI workflow failures often come from structural conditions.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/issues/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Issues</p>
          <h2>Browse visible failure surfaces</h2>
          <p>Issues describe real-world symptoms in plain language and map them to structural patterns.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-section">
      <h2>Recently added</h2>
      <div class="wb-row-list">
        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/issues/actual-policy-differs-from-declared-policy/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Issue</p>
          <h2>Actual Policy Differs From Declared Policy</h2>
          <p>The policy the AI or workflow actually follows differs from the policy that is documented, declared, displayed, or expected.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/lenses/conflict-lens/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Lens</p>
          <h2>Conflict Lens</h2>
          <p>Detects mutually incompatible constraints, claims, states, or declarations that cannot be simultaneously satisfied.</p>
        </a>

        <a class="wb-row" href="/workbench/patterns/circular-dependency/">
          <p class="wb-row-meta">Pattern</p>
          <h2>Circular Dependency</h2>
          <p>A structural condition where two or more elements depend on each other in a closed loop without an independent base condition.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</WorkbenchLayout>
